  "description": "PUTRIG crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C48 H68 O32 Tm6 6+,6(Cl1 1-),18(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tm1 (Tm) has 8 O neighbors; Tm2 (Tm) has 8 O neighbors; Tm3 (Tm) has 8 O neighbors; Tm1A (Tm) has 8 O neighbors; Tm2A (Tm) has 8 O neighbors; Tm3A (Tm) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 7 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.466-3.702 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.95-110.04°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Tm6(μ3-OH)4L4L′2(H2O)10]Cl6·18H2O (L = o-vanillinate; L′ = 2-hydroxymethyl-6-methoxyphenolate); C48H104Cl6O50Tm6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 10 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 10 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
